# Chapter 1, Strings in formulas: a formula that begins with a quotation
# mark is a label; begin it with a plus sign instead (columns 20 wide)
do /wgc20~
A1 Initech
A2 "Initech"&" 123"
show A2
A3 +"Initech"&" 123"
show A3
= +A1&" 123"
= @UPPER(A1)
= @LENGTH(A1)
= +A1="Initech"
= +A1="initech"
= @EXACT(A1,"initech")
= +"abc"<"abd"
